---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Riviera News"
  description="Local news for Azizi Riviera residents — what's actually changing in the development, not another citywide press release."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">News</p>
    <h1>What's changing in Riviera</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Dubai has no shortage of citywide news coverage already. This page is
      for the other kind: what's actually changing inside Riviera itself —
      not events (see the <a href="/events/">events page</a> for those),
      but the ongoing state of the development.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What counts as news here</h2>
    <p>
      New promenade tenants opening, phases of the development completing,
      changes to building management or amenities, and anything else that
      changes what it's actually like to live in Riviera. Citywide stories
      get plenty of coverage elsewhere; this page deliberately doesn't
      duplicate that.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Follow along</h2>
    <p>
      The fastest-moving version of this lives on Instagram
      (<strong>@rivieradst</strong>) rather than here — this page is the
      durable, searchable record, while the Instagram account is where it
      happens first.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
